{"causes": ["The counterculture movements of the 1960s and 1970s emphasized holistic approaches to health and consciousness.", "Advancements in recording technology allowed for the creation and distribution of ambient and electronic music.", "The rise of wellness culture and practices such as yoga and meditation created a demand for soothing and inspirational music."], "effects": ["New age music has influenced the development of various subgenres, including chill-out and ambient music.", "It has become a significant component of the wellness industry, with millions using it for meditation and relaxation.", "The genre has facilitated the global spread of alternative spiritual practices and holistic health approaches."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "new-age-music", "sourceName": "New Age Music", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "wellness-culture", "targetName": "Wellness Culture", "context": "New age music significantly influences wellness culture, providing a soundtrack for practices like meditation and yoga."}, {"sourceSlug": "ambient-music", "sourceName": "Ambient Music", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "new-age-music", "targetName": "New Age Music", "context": "Ambient music serves as a foundational element in the creation of new age music, emphasizing soundscapes over traditional musical structures."}, {"sourceSlug": "yoga", "sourceName": "Yoga", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "new-age-music", "targetName": "New Age Music", "context": "Yoga sessions frequently incorporate new age music to enhance the experience of relaxation and mindfulness."}, {"sourceSlug": "new-age-music-conference", "sourceName": "New Age Music Conference", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "los-angeles", "targetName": "Los Angeles", "context": "The New Age Music Conference occurs annually in Los Angeles, showcasing artists and promoting the genre since the 1990s."}, {"sourceSlug": "environmentalism", "sourceName": "Environmentalism", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "new-age-music", "targetName": "New Age Music", "context": "New age music often collaborates with environmentalism, reflecting themes of nature and ecological awareness in its compositions."}], "places": [{"name": "Los Angeles, USA", "role": "Cultural Hub"}, {"name": "Dublin, Ireland", "role": "Birthplace of Enya"}, {"name": "Athens, Greece", "role": "Home of Vangelis"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: new age music", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "new-age-music"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q213121", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New-age_music"], "tags": ["music genre", "Music & Compositions", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "new age music contributed to the historical record of the Contemporary period. Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "New age music has significantly shaped contemporary wellness practices, influencing millions globally and contributing to a cultural shift towards mindfulness and holistic health.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-21T01:05:28Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#29791980571", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "New age is a genre of music intended to create artistic inspiration, relaxation, and optimism. It is used by listeners for yoga, massage, meditation, and reading as a method of stress management to bring about a state of ecstasy rather than trance, or to create a peaceful atmosphere in homes or other environments. It is sometimes associated with environmentalism and New Age spirituality; however, most of its artists have nothing to do with "New Age spirituality", and some even reject the term. new age music is a music genre, created circa 1960. A moderately significant entity in the historical record. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "New age music emerged in the late 20th century, primarily in the United States and Europe, as a distinct genre that blends elements of ambient, electronic, and acoustic sounds, aiming to evoke emotional tranquility and spiritual awareness. Its roots can be traced back to the countercultural movements of the 1960s and 1970s, which sought alternative approaches to consciousness and healing, thus reflecting broader societal shifts towards holistic lifestyles and environmental awareness. Key figures in this genre include artists such as Enya, Yanni, and Vangelis, who have popularized new age music worldwide, making it a staple in yoga studios, spas, and relaxation playlists.

The genre gained notable traction with the release of albums like 'Watermark' by Enya in 1988, which sold over 3 million copies in the United States alone, and 'Themes' by Vangelis, which became synonymous with cinematic soundscapes. The proliferation of new age music was facilitated by advancements in recording technology and the establishment of new music distribution channels, including dedicated radio stations and later, online platforms. Festivals such as the 'New Age Music Conference' have also played a crucial role in promoting the genre and its artists, creating a community around shared values of peace and healing.

The legacy of new age music is apparent in its lasting impact on various cultural and artistic movements, influencing genres such as chill-out and electronic music, while also permeating wellness and mindfulness practices. This genre has created a cultural footprint that continues to resonate, with millions of listeners worldwide using it as a backdrop for meditation and relaxation. The phrase 'Music is the universal language of mankind' aptly summarizes its role in fostering a sense of global connection through shared auditory experiences."}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-21T01:05:28Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#29791980571", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": ["Cultural, artistic, or intellectual creation"], "newValue": ["The counterculture movements of the 1960s and 1970s emphasized holistic approaches to health and consciousness.", "Advancements in recording technology allowed for the creation and distribution of ambient and electronic music.", "The rise of wellness culture and practices such as yoga and meditation created a demand for soothing and inspirational music."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-21T01:05:28Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#29791980571", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": ["Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission"], "newValue": ["New age music has influenced the development of various subgenres, including chill-out and ambient music.", "It has become a significant component of the wellness industry, with millions using it for meditation and relaxation.", "The genre has facilitated the global spread of alternative spiritual practices and holistic health approaches."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-21T01:05:28Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#29791980571", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "new-age-music", "sourceName": "new age music", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "era-contemporary", "targetName": "Contemporary", "context": "new age music is situated within the Conte